## 9️⃣ Performance & UX Enhancements

| Feature | How to Implement |
|---------|------------------|
| **Lazy Load Images** | Use `<img loading="lazy">` or a library like `react-lazy-load-image-component`. |
| **Skeleton Screens** | Show placeholders while data loads (`react-loading-skeleton`). |
| **Optimistic Updates** | With React Query, use `mutationFn` + `onMutate` to update UI before server confirms. |
| **Code Splitting** | Dynamic imports (`React.lazy`) for heavy pages. |
| **Accessibility** | Semantic HTML, ARIA labels, keyboard focus management. |
| **SEO** | Server‑side rendering (Next.js/Nuxt.js) or prerender static pages (SvelteKit). |

---

## 🔟 Deployment

| Platform | Steps |
|----------|-------|
| **Netlify** | Connect repo → Set build command (`npm run build`) → Deploy. |
| **Vercel** | Same as Netlify; great for Next.js/Nuxt.js. |
| **Render** | Static site hosting + optional backend services. |
| **Docker** | Containerize with `Dockerfile`, push to Docker Hub, deploy to any container host. |

Example `Dockerfile` for Vite:

```dockerfile
FROM node:20-alpine AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci
COPY . .
RUN npm run build

FROM nginx:alpine
COPY --from=builder /app/dist /usr/share/nginx/html
EXPOSE 80
CMD ["nginx", "-g", "daemon off;"]
```

